.TH "ELSERENO\-SCOPE" "5" "2026\-04\-19" "ElSereno scope file" "File formats"
.SH NAME
\f[B]scope.yaml\f[R]: authorised scope file for \f[I]elsereno\f[R](1)
.SH DESCRIPTION
A \f[I]scope.yaml\f[R] file defines the authorised ranges, ports and
protocols, the serve bind allow\-list and the dialling blacklist, for an
engagement.
It also accepts a canary, which is parsed but not applied.
.PP
A scope file applies only when passed with \f[B]\-\-scope\f[R].
Every command that connects to a target takes it: \f[B]scan\f[R],
\f[B]serve\f[R] (dashboard, API and schedule scans), \f[B]discover\f[R],
\f[B]fingerprint probe\f[R], \f[B]plaintext\-check\f[R], \f[B]tui
\-\-input\f[R], \f[B]opcua probe\-anon\f[R] and \f[B]probe\-write\f[R],
\f[B]s7 probe\f[R], \f[B]probe\-protection\f[R] and
\f[B]probe\-identity\f[R], and in the offensive build \f[B]write modbus
send\f[R], \f[B]exploit run\f[R], \f[B]proxy listen\f[R],
\f[B]harvest\f[R] and \f[B]creds\-check http\f[R], plus \f[B]dial\f[R]
(which applies only \f[B]dial.blocked_numbers\f[R]).
\f[B]lint \-\-scope\f[R] only validates it.
Until 2026\-10\-17 only \f[B]scan\f[R], \f[B]serve\f[R] and
\f[B]dial\f[R] took it.
Nothing loads it on its own: a \f[I]scope.yaml\f[R] in the working
directory is not read, and without \f[B]\-\-scope\f[R] nothing is
filtered.
A file that does not parse stops the command with exit 78.
Keys other than the ones below are a parse error, and a range
\f[B]cidr\f[R] that does not parse or a port outside 0..65535 is
rejected at load too (PITF\-097), so \f[B]lint \-\-scope\f[R] catches a
typo that would otherwise narrow the scope in silence.
.SH FORMAT
.IP
.EX
